  {
   "index": 14,
   "start": 128.767,
   "duration": 30.4,
   "end": 159.167,
   "text": "Those misses fall up or down at random, so they partly cancel. [pause 0.3] Sixteen darts typically stray four halves, not sixteen. [pause 0.3] What adds is their squares: sixteen of them fill a square four halves wide. [pause 0.4] N darts stray about root N halves. [pause 0.3] Divide by N, and the typical miss is a half over root N. [pause 0.8] For a hundred darts: five points. We measured four point eight. [pause 0.3] Any other function swaps the half for its own spread, sigma; there's still no d.",
